      "directNodeIds": [
        "math:factorial-notation"
      ],
      "explanation": "For a positive integer \\(n\\), the factorial \\(n!\\) is the product of the integers from \\(1\\) through \\(n\\). First evaluate the factorial inside the parentheses: \\(3!=3\\cdot2\\cdot1=6\\). Therefore,\n\\[\n\\frac{(3!)!}{3!}\n=\\frac{6!}{3!}\n=\\frac{6\\cdot5\\cdot4\\cdot3!}{3!}\n=6\\cdot5\\cdot4=120.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(120\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
      "id": "evaluate-nested-factorial",
